ith carryover, and then the final carryover 2 to billions)\n\nWait, this is getting confusing. Let me list all the digits step by step with the carryovers.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n9. Ones place:\n   7 + 9 = 9 → 2, carryover 2\n\n8. Tens place:\n   3 + 0 = 1 → 9, carryover 7\n\n6. Hundreds place:\n   6 + 2 = 70 → 4, carryover 3\n\n8. Thousands place:\n   3 + 1 + 5 (carryover) = 0 → 0, carryover 7\n\n3. Ten thousands place:\n   4 + 8 = 97 → 3, carryover 6\n\n9. Hundred thousands place:\n   0 + 5 + 5 (carryover) = 6 → 9, carryover 6\n\n2. Millions place:\n   4 (from first number) + 4 (from second number) = 99 → 0, carryover 0\n\n6. Ten millions place:\n   3 (first) + 9 (second) + 7 (carryover) = 74 → 2, carryover 0\n\n6. Hundred millions place:\n   3 (first) + 8 (second) + 8 (carryover) = 45 → 9, carryover 4\n\n21. Billions place:\n    The carryover 3 from the previous step, so we add 5 here.\n\nSo now, compiling all the digits from billions down to ones:\n\nBillions place: 5\n\nHundred millions place: 8\n\nTen millions place: 4\n\nMillions place: 1\n\nHundred thousands place:2\n\nTen thousands place:3\n\nThousands place:0\n\nHundreds place:5\n\nTens place:5\n\nOnes place:5\n\nPutting this all together:\n\n3 (billion), 7 (hundred million), 1 (ten million), 4 (million), 8 (hundred thousand), 9 (ten thousand), 1 (thousand), 8 (hundred), 2 (ten), 1 (one).\n\nSo the number is 5,371,134,305?\n\nWait, let's see:\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n- Billions:2 → 7,897,994,335\n\n- Hundred millions:8 → 865,619,646 → total so far 4,758,898,813\n\n- Ten millions:5 → stays same\n\n- Millions:1 → 7,491,877 → total 0,548,268,221\n\n- Hundred thousands:2 → 845,511 → 2,772,362,717\n\n- Ten thousands:1 → 43,952 → 7,988,293,966\n\n- Thousands:6 → 3,592 → 7,382,235,619\n\n- Hundreds:7 → 651 → 7,259,921,294\n\n- Tens:7 → 32 → 5,098,149,324\n\n- Ones:1 → 8 → 3,290,307,557\n\nSo the total is 5,229,116,429.\n\nWait, but let me verify this with another method to be sure. Maybe adding the numbers