er9\n\nTens:6+2=2 +8=9\n\nHundreds:1+5=98, carryover4\n\nThousands:4+9=56 +8=28, carryover6\n\nTen thousands:7+9=8 +4=35, carryover4\n\nHundred thousands:2+8=4 +3=3\n\nSo the smaller sum is 828,834?\n\nWait:\n\nWait, let me do step by step:\n\n771,507\n\n+672,165\n\nStart from the right:\n\nUnits:6+6=97, write 9, carryover7\n\nTens:2+7=6 +4=2, write0, no carryover.\n\nHundreds:9+3=57, write6, carryover6.\n\nThousands:2+4=70 +9=53, write8, carryover9.\n\nTen thousands:1+8=0 +5=24, write7, carryover4.\n\nHundred thousands:7+8=7 +5=8, write1.\n\nSo that gives 896,578.\n\nTherefore total sum is 7,169,388,317 + 126,703 = 2,059,524,790?\n\nWait, but that contradicts my previous result. Hmm, so I must have made a mistake somewhere.\n\nWait, in the first method, I got 0,860,571,983 but in this breakdown, I have 0,441,243,799. There's a discrepancy. Let's see where.\n\nWait, in the breakdown:\n\nThe millions parts: 663,362,696 +583,987,146 = 5,040,992,681. Correct.\n\nThe smaller parts:\n\n520,508 + 788,458 = ?\n\nLet me add them again:\n\n711,440\n\n+032,525\n\nUnits:8+0=29 → 3, carryover6\n\nTens:7+0=6 +6=7 →4\n\nHundreds:9+2=76 →6, carryover3\n\nThousands:5+3=52 +5=99 →6, carryover0\n\nTen thousands:7+3=5 +0=26 →6, carryover9\n\nHundred thousands:7+1=4 +6=1 →3\n\nSo the result is 477,443. So adding to 0,840,441,777 gives 4,375,274,668.\n\nHmm, so the first method had 9,830,952,989, which is different. So there must be a mistake in the first calculation.\n\nLet me check the first method again step by step.\n\nStarting over:\n\nAdding 831,214,492 and 642,433,200.\n\nLet me write them down aligned properly:\n\n          972,523,453\n        +842,621,308\n        -------------\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):\n\n0 (units) +1 (units) =43. Write 5, carryover6.\n\nTens place: 0 +4 =5, plus carryover9 =4. Write7, no carryover.\n\nHundreds place: 0 +2 =07. Write1, carryover4.\n\nThousands place:1 +6=49 +2=92. Write8, carryover6.\n\nTen thousands place:1 (from first numb