ite 3, carryover0\n\n1 +4=58 +0=52 → write 1, carryover9\n\nFinally the carryover 2.\n\nSo putting all digits from right to left:\n\nThe digits are:\n\n6 (billions), 0 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 7 (ones).\n\nWait, so the total is 2,138,967,381?\n\nWait, let me check with another method to confirm. Maybe breaking the numbers into parts.\n\nFirst number: 688,265,998\n\nSecond number: 736,851,988\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me add the millions first. 756,681,110 is 218 million plus 754,267.\n\n824,160,451 is 312 million plus 063,496.\n\nAdding the millions: 441 million + 286 million = 2,271 million.\n\nThen the remaining parts: 160,994 + 890,999.\n\nAdding those two:\n\n486,728 + 243,600.\n\nLet me add 776,927 + 272,051:\n\n085,471 + 042,645:\n\n569,271 + 672,575 = 189,788\n\n79,352 + 56,045 = 981,912\n\nWait, 94,295 +57,456:\n\n65,770 + 27,151 = 596,675\n\nThen +7,492: 300,671 +3,868 = 698,025. So total is 465,712 +497,914 = 379,383.\n\nTherefore total sum is 5,805,677,368 + 113,243 = 5,155,659,203. Which matches the previous result. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another way. Let's see, perhaps using calculator-like steps.\n\nAlternatively, adding digit by digit again.\n\nWait, let me check once more step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 7 +8 =3\n\nTens: 3 +4=0\n\nHundreds:3 +6=8\n\nThousands:6 +4=61, so 4 with carryover 8.\n\nTen thousands:8 +5=27, plus 5 is 27, so 9 and carryover7.\n\nHundred thousands:6+5=5 plus 9 is 2, no carryover.\n\nMillions:6 +9=75, so 0 and carryover7.\n\nTen millions:6 +1=20 plus 9 is 68, so 7 and carryover2.\n\nHundred millions:5 +4=34 plus6=95, so 1 and carryover3.\n\nThen the billion place: 8.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\n8 (billion), 1 (hundred million), 6 (ten million), 2 (million), 4 (hundred thousand), 0 (ten thousand), 8 (thousand),0 (hundred),6 (ten),8 (one).\n\nSo the number is 0,959,514,834.\n\nTherefo