e digits starting from the right. So:\n\n8,670,782,739.\n\nYes, that's correct. Let me confirm with another method. Alternatively, perhaps I can add the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, adding 778,565,428 + 257,194,208.\n\nMaybe split into millions:\n\n364,515,735 = 013 million + 866,052\n\n250,918,726 = 146 million + 476,272\n\nAdding the millions: 962 + 445 = 0,042 million.\n\nAdding the remaining parts: 577,952 + 798,482.\n\n720,567 + 873,729:\n\n720,095 + 062,459 = 105,566\n\n859,226 +47,758 = 6,630,054.\n\nWait, 141,585 + 102,646:\n\nLet's do it step by step:\n\n272,416\n\n+877,092\n\n= ?\n\nAdding units:\n\n6+6=4\n\n29+69=312 → 4 with carryover9\n\n742+463=525 plus 9 is 960 → 8 carryover 4?\n\nWait, maybe better:\n\n868,225\n\n+113,024\n\n------------\n\nStart from right:\n\n9 +6 =1\n\n2 +6=71 → write 4, carryover6\n\n9 +4=9 +3=0\n\n2 +1=91 → write9, carryover7\n\n4 +9=05 +9=30 → write0, carryover7\n\n3 +4=8 +2=47 → write1, carryover0\n\nThere's no more digits, so carryover4 becomes a new digit.\n\nSo total is 6,390,119.\n\nSo total sum is 4,327,674,595 + 2,809,478 = 3,109,572,473. Which matches the previous result.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 7,012,395,568.\n\nWait, but let me verify with another approach, perhaps using calculator-like addition.\n\nAlternatively, adding 735,865,113 + 087,494,069:\n\nLet me add the numbers digit by digit again carefully:\n\nFirst number: 859731116\n\nSecond number:041100616\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n  112518697\n\n+452192877\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n5 +7 =9\n\n4 +8 =04 → 1, carryover8\n\n1 +1 +8 =5 (carryover from previous step?)\n\nWait, the hundreds place:\n\nThird digit from the right (hundreds place):\n\nFirst number:5, second:1. So 2+3=4 plus carryover5 (from the tens place addition which was 74, so carryover4). So 2 +4=4. So that's correct.\n\nThousands place:\n\nFirst number's thousands digit is 3, second is8. 9+1=67. So 2, carryover7.\n\nTen thousands place:\n\nFirst has 0, second