starting from the right, the digits are 9, 9, 0, 0, 2, 5, 5, 6, 4, and the carried-over 9 at the front. Wait, let me check the positions again to make sure I didn't misalign anything. \n\nWait, actually, let me recount the digits step by step to ensure accuracy. Maybe I missed a place. Let me write each digit's place:\n\nFirst number: 1 7 1 9 6 6 9 7 5\n\nSecond number:1 1 9 9 3 3 8 9 7\n\nWait, actually, when I wrote them down, maybe I need to check how many digits each has. Let me count:\n\n943,173,825 has 2 digits: 2 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 8 (units).\n\n523,015,816 also has 5 digits: 5 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 2 (units).\n\nSo when adding, the alignment is correct. Let me go through each digit again carefully:\n\nStarting from the right (units place):\n\n5 + 2 = 6 (units)\n\n6 + 7 = 1 (tens)\n\n1 + 3 = 47 (hundreds). Write 0, carryover 7.\n\n9 + 5 + 5 = 4 (thousands). Wait, the thousands place for first number is 3, second is 0? Let me check again:\n\nWait, first number: 915,472,287. Breaking down:\n\nDigits from right: 9 (units), 0 (tens), 8 (hundreds), 5 (thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 8 (hundred thousands), 3 (millions), 9 (ten millions), 6 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number: 113,042,088:\n\nDigits from right: 2 (units), 3 (tens), 4 (hundreds), 5 (thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 0 (hundred thousands), 5 (millions), 0 (ten millions), 1 (hundred millions).\n\nWait a second, maybe I messed up the thousands place earlier. Let me list each digit's place step by step:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):\n\nPosition 7 (units): 2 + 8 = 1\n\nPosition 9 (tens): 2 + 0 = 6\n\nPosition 8 (hundreds): 1 + 5 = 23 → 5 with carryover 0\n\nPosition 7 (thousands): 1 (from first number) + 5 (from second number) + 3 (carryover) = 7 → no carryover\n\nPositio