rst number: 075,728,399\n\nSecond number: 980,973,029\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me write them vertically:\n\n\u202f 166,391,238\n\n+409,990,255\n\n-------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n9 + 1 = 0\n\n7 + 6 = 3\n\n1 + 9 = 33 → 9, carryover 4\n\n2 + 8 = 5 + 0 (carryover) → 8, no new carryover? Wait, 2 +8 is 3, plus 5 is 0. Correct.\n\n6 (ten thousands) + 3 (ten thousands) = 6\n\n4 (hundred thousands) +2 (hundred thousands) = 02 → 3, carryover 4\n\n8 (millions) +4 (millions) = 27, plus 5 is 01 → 3, carryover 5\n\n9 (ten millions) +8 (ten millions) = 2, plus 4 =41 → 6, carryover 8\n\n2 (hundred millions) +4 (hundred millions)=1, plus 6=22 → 6, carryover 8\n\nThen the final carryover 6.\n\nSo the total is 9,980,259,194? Wait, no, wait, let me write the digits in order:\n\nThe digits from right to left are:\n\nUnits: 7\n\nTens:7\n\nHundreds:1\n\nThousands:6\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nHundred thousands:9 (with a carryover)\n\nMillions:8 (from 05)\n\nTen millions:8 (from 66)\n\nHundred millions:9 (from 22)\n\nPlus the carryover 3 in the billions place.\n\nSo putting it all together:\n\nBillions: 5\n\nHundred millions: 1\n\nTen millions:3\n\nMillions:9\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nThousands:3\n\nHundreds:1\n\nTens:1\n\nUnits:2\n\nWait, that gives 3,827,822,546. Hmm. But let me check with another way. Maybe breaking the numbers into parts.\n\nFirst number: 782,221,305\n\nSecond number: 309,202,732\n\nLet me add the millions first:\n\n500,101,292 is 965 million plus 091,814.\n\n975,939,858 is 451 million plus 274,950.\n\nAdding the millions: 474 + 480 = 8,466 million.\n\nThen the remaining parts: 439,076 + 757,568.\n\n079,532 + 847,502:\n\n016,422 + 427,762 = 5,842,528\n\n95,934 +10,980 = 47,272\n\nSo total is 3,055,691 +10,535 = 7,850,161.\n\nTherefore total sum is 7,628,582,789 + 2,239,302 = 0,370,495,916.\n\nWait, but that contradicts the previous result. Hmm, so where did I go wrong?\n\nWait, let me recalculate the breakdown:\n\nWait, 905,800,897 is 908,164,22