ve from previous steps.\n\nPutting it all together:\n\nStarting from the highest digit now:\n\nBillions place:7\n\nHundred millions:7\n\nTen millions:2\n\nMillions:1\n\nHundred thousands:5\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nThousands:6\n\nHundreds:2\n\nTens:3\n\nUnits:5\n\nSo writing the number:\n\n9,030,705,776?\n\nWait, let me arrange the digits properly.\n\nWait, let's list all the digits from highest to lowest:\n\nBillions:9\n\nHundred millions:6\n\nTen millions:5\n\nMillions:4\n\nHundred thousands:1\n\nTen thousands:8\n\nThousands:8\n\nHundreds:0\n\nTens:7\n\nUnits:8\n\nSo combining these:\n\n2 (billion), 9 (hundred million), 8 (ten million), 4 (million), 7 (hundred thousand), 4 (ten thousand), 5 (thousand), 7 (hundred), 0 (ten), 6 (unit).\n\nSo the number is 5,696,007,174?\n\nWait, let me check the placement again:\n\nBreaking down each digit position's result:\n\nPosition3 (hundred millions):7\n\nPosition7 (ten millions):4 (from the ten millions place which was 6 after carryover?)\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the positions.\n\nWait let me reconstruct the number step by step:\n\nAfter adding each position, the digits from right to left (units to billions) are:\n\nUnits:7\n\nTens:9\n\nHundreds:6\n\nThousands:9\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nMillions:7\n\nTen millions:7\n\nHundred millions:6\n\nBillions:4 (due to the final carryover)\n\nSo arranging from left (billions) to right (units):\n\nBillions digit:7\n\nHundred millions:9\n\nTen millions:9\n\nMillions:7\n\nHundred thousands:0\n\nTen thousands:6\n\nThousands:6\n\nHundreds:8\n\nTens:6\n\nUnits:5\n\nTherefore the number is:\n\n0,290,893,854.\n\nWait, let me verify this with another method to ensure I didn't make an error.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add the numbers in parts.\n\nFirst number:629,373,507\n\nSecond number:808,629,719\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me separate into millions, thousands, and units.\n\nFirst number breakdown:\n\n891,271,885 = 238,951,349 + 974,982\n\nSecond number:908,796,581 = 