s):\n\n2 +4=3\n\nPosition6 (millions):\n\n7 +8=8\n\nPosition1 (hundred thousands):\n\n4 +0=5? Wait hold on.\n\nWait, maybe I'm misaligning the digits. Let me clarify each digit's place:\n\nFirst number breakdown:\n\nDigit positions (from right, 5 to0):\n\nPosition0:9 (units)\n\nPosition3:9 (tens)\n\nPosition5:6 (hundreds)\n\nPosition8:0 (thousands)\n\nPosition4:9 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition2:4 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition0:5 (millions)\n\nPosition5:2 (ten millions)\n\nPosition2:5 (hundred millions)\n\nSecond number:\n\nPosition0:3 (units)\n\nPosition4:8 (tens)\n\nPosition0:7 (hundreds)\n\nPosition9:1 (thousands)\n\nPosition3:8 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition0:1 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition3:0 (millions)\n\nPosition7:9 (ten millions)\n\nPosition5:2 (hundred millions)\n\nTherefore, when adding each position:\n\nPosition9:8+6=4\n\nPosition8:7+4=6\n\nPosition2:1+8=43 →2 with carryover9\n\nPosition2:5 +2 +2=5\n\nPosition4:8 +0=80 →8 with carryover8\n\nPosition5:6 +3 +5=1\n\nPosition2:3 +9=7\n\nPosition3:2 +4=7\n\nPosition5:5 +2=2\n\nThus the total is 4 9 4 5 3 0 9 4 4 → 219,732,339.\n\nWait but when adding the remaining parts (the 233,709 and 691,545), I get 528,528. So why is there a difference?\n\nWait, perhaps the breakdown is wrong because the 425,450 is not the last six digits? Wait, let me see:\n\nThe first number is 885,934,749. Breaking down into millions:\n\nThe first three digits (226) are hundred millions, ten millions, millions.\n\nThe next three digits (420) are hundred thousands, ten thousands, thousands.\n\nThe last three digits (378) are hundreds, tens, units.\n\nTherefore, 714,448 is the last six digits, which are hundred thousands down to units. So adding the two numbers' remaining parts (excluding the millions):\n\nFirst number's remaining:237,158\n\nSecond number's remaining:521,666\n\nAdding those:152,275 +393,045 = 970,947. Correct.\n\nThus total sum is 756,966,386 +740,520 =776,279,869.\n\nBut according to digit-by-digit, it's 278,258,293. There's a contradiction here. \n\nWait, what is the actual sum of 384,686 and 880,614?\n\nLet me compute this separately:\n\n807,505\n\n+110,914\n\n------------\n\nAdding units:9+4=8\n\nTens:6+8=0\n\nHundreds:3+8=76 →8 carryover4\n\nThousands:2+5 +5=3\n\nTen thousands:6 +0=75 →8 carryover3\n\nHundred thousands:3 +5 +2=5\n\nSo total is 423,798. So that's correct.\n\nSo why is the digit-by-digit method giving a different result?\n\nWait, maybe in the digit-by-digit method, the positions are being counted incorrectly. Let me re-express the digit-by-digit result properly.\n\nThe digit-by-digit method gave digits from position2 to position0 as:\n\nPosition2:3 (hundred millions)\n\nPosition4:4 (ten millions)\n\nPosition2:8 (millions)\n\nPosition0:7 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition1:9 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition1:7 (thousands)\n\nPosition9:5 (hundreds)\n\nPosition4:7 (tens)\n\nPosition7:0 (units)\n\nTherefore, the number is:\n\n9 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions),3 (millions),\n\n0 (hundred thousands),9 (ten thousands),5 (thousands),\n\n9 (hundreds),7 (tens),7 (units).\n\nSo written out as 624,329,568.\n\nWait, but according to the breakdown, it should be 157,551,993. The difference is in the hundred thousands, ten thousands, thousands places: 377,214 vs 459,446.\n\nAh! I see now. The digit-by-digit method's hundred thousands place is 3, ten thousands is 4, thousands is3, so combined it's 643,963. Wait, no:\n\nWait the hundred thousands digit is position0:6 (so 082,871)\n\nten thousands digit is position0:6 (so 06,653)\n\nthousands digit is position2:3 (so 0,477)\n\nTherefore, 331,258 +46,736 +0,997 =582,325. Exactly matching the breakdown. \n\nWait then why is the digit-by-digit result written as 109,799,318?\n\nWait, if the hundred thousands digit is 5, ten thousands is 6, thousands is7, that is 135,239. So the number should be 741,699,585. But according to the digit-by-digit digits, it's 390,674,115. \n\nWait, this is the confusion. How are the digits grouped?\n\nThe digits