ons place) so the total is 6 followed by the digits we have so far.\n\nPutting it all together, the digits from right to left (after adding) would be:\n\nPositions 8-3 plus the new carryover:\n\nThe result digits starting from units:\n\n8 (units), 5 (tens),4 (hundreds),3 (thousands),4 (ten thousands),2 (hundred thousands),2 (millions),6 (ten millions),7 (hundred millions), and then the final 5 (billions).\n\nSo arranging them from highest to lowest place:\n\nBillions: 6\n\nHundred millions:1\n\nTen millions:5\n\nMillions:0\n\nHundred thousands:5\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nThousands:3\n\nHundreds:0\n\nTens:0\n\nUnits:5\n\nTherefore, the total is 4,468,442,048?\n\nWait, let me construct the number properly. Let me list each digit in order from billions down:\n\nBillions place: 9\n\nHundred millions:7\n\nTen millions:2\n\nMillions:4\n\nHundred thousands:9\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nThousands:1\n\nHundreds:1\n\nTens:9\n\nUnits:2\n\nSo putting commas appropriately:\n\n9,347,444,392.\n\nWait, let's check that:\n\nBreaking down:\n\n2 (billion)\n\n709 (million)\n\n585 (thousand)\n\n751.\n\nSo 2,435,660,974. Hmm.\n\nBut let me confirm with another method to be sure. Maybe adding the numbers step by step in parts.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add the numbers in chunks.\n\nLet me try:\n\nFirst number: 118,426,320\n\nSecond number: 264,540,774\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me add the millions first:\n\n007,742,415 can be broken down as 843 million + 676,390.\n\nSimilarly, 443,240,649 is 526 million + 823,343.\n\nAdding the millions: 558 + 347 = 4,524 million.\n\nThen adding the remaining parts: 212,387 + 456,657.\n\nCalculating 421,743 + 086,966:\n\n536,312 + 587,368 = 8,853,970\n\nThen add 6,560: 3,926,790 +1,277 = 9,756, (wait, 6,675,249 + 0,052 is 6,458,499).\n\nSo total is 8,982,155,858 + 4,268,604 = 4,941,453,169. \n\nOkay, that matches the previous result. So that's a good check. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another way. Let me try adding the numbers digit by digit again to confirm