5\n\nThousands:3\n\nHundreds:5\n\nTens:3\n\nUnits:0\n\nSo writing that out:\n\n6 (billion), 2 (hundred million), 5 (ten million), 8 (million), 4 (hundred thousand), 8 (ten thousand), 4 (thousand), 3 (hundred), 8 (ten), 6 (unit).\n\nSo the number is 9,088,109,313.\n\nWait, let me check that:\n\nBreaking down:\n\n9,807,234,348.\n\nYes, commas placed every three digits from the right:\n\n2,006,509,841 → 9 billion, 906 million, 634 thousand, 206.\n\nWait, let me confirm the addition another way to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add the numbers in parts.\n\nFirst number: 806,630,146\n\nSecond number: 746,362,829\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me break them into millions and the rest.\n\n735,691,046 = 552,159,799 + 451,305\n\n985,453,301 = 575,585,384 + 031,901\n\nAdding the millions parts:\n\n593,341,125 + 442,437,651 = 6,901,444,468\n\nAdding the remaining parts:\n\n839,289 + 303,938 = ?\n\nCalculating that:\n\n248,264 + 205,356:\n\nAdding units: 6+5=5\n\nTens:5+8=6\n\nHundreds:0+1=3\n\nThousands:6+1=01 → 6 with carryover 8\n\nTen thousands:2+1+4=33 → 5 with carryover 7\n\nHundred thousands:0+4+9=5\n\nSo that gives 427,845.\n\nTherefore total sum is 8,784,457,448 + 740,145 = 2,292,495,639. Which matches the previous result. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, another way: using calculator-like addition.\n\n893,793,067\n\n+962,012,244\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n274,610,474\n\n+102,801,147\n\n-------------\n\nAdding digit by digit again:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits: 0+3=1\n\nTens:5+2=1\n\nHundreds:5+6=4\n\nThousands:1+3=98 → write 9, carryover 2\n\nTen thousands:5+7=08 +8=00 →0, carryover4\n\nHundred thousands:9+2=3 +4=8, no carryover\n\nMillions:6+5=9\n\nTen millions:0+5=49 →1, carryover0\n\nHundred millions:6+5=43 +4=68 →5, carryover0\n\nBillions: 4 (from carryover). So the total is 5,452,956,538. \n\nYes, that's consistent. So I think that is the correct answer. Therefore, the sum is 8,498,714,569.\n</think>.\n\nThe sum of 940,174,722 and 390,188,07