number)=90. So write down 6 in millions place and carryover 5 to the next (ten millions).\n\n7. Ten millions place: 7 (first number) +1 (second number) +0 (carryover)=3. So 4 here, no new carryover.\n\n1. Hundred millions place: 5 (first number) +5 (second number)=96. So write down 4 in hundred millions and carryover 8 to the billions place.\n\n64. Billions place: The carryover 8 from the hundred millions, so we have 2 in the billions place.\n\nNow, compiling all the digits from highest to lowest:\n\nBillions:4\n\nHundred millions:2\n\nTen millions:0\n\nMillions:3\n\nHundred thousands:7\n\nTen thousands:6\n\nThousands:2\n\nHundreds:9\n\nTens:3\n\nOnes:9\n\nSo putting all together, the number is:\n\n7,9 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 9 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 4 (ones).\n\nTherefore, the full number is 2,740,323,276?\n\nWait, let me check the commas. Let me structure it with commas properly.\n\nStarting from the right, every three digits:\n\nBillions: 8\n\nThen hundred millions, ten millions, millions: 484 (since 3 (billion), then 8 hundred millions, 4 ten millions, 9 million). Wait, perhaps breaking into sections:\n\nThe number is:\n\n6,984,949,281\n\nWait, let's see:\n\nBillions digit: 0\n\nThen the next three digits (hundred millions, ten millions, millions): 4,1,2 → 900\n\nThen the next three (hundred thousands, ten thousands, thousands): 6,9,0 → 962\n\nThen the last three (hundreds, tens, ones): 9,0,7 → 291\n\nSo combining with commas: 9,695,713,412.\n\nHmm, let me verify this with another method to ensure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers step by step:\n\nFirst number: 330,736,763\n\nSecond number: 809,494,917\n\nAdding them:\n\nStart with the first number: 891,994,104\n\nAdd 311,696,533 to it: 367,703,622 + 743,952,199 = 8,753,671,201\n\nThen add the remaining 60,645,446:\n\n9,435,402,337 + 01,151,244\n\nFirst add 09,622,718: 4,460,938,703 + 35,191,739 = 8,21