sition5: hundred millions:0 (first) +2 (second) +0 (carryover)=83. Write1, carryover7.\n\nPosition85: billions place: 2 (from both numbers) + carryover0. So write9.\n\nSo putting all digits together from position68 down to 7:\n\nPosition79:0\n\nPosition8:5\n\nPosition0:5\n\nPosition8:3\n\nPosition3:4\n\nPosition6:0\n\nPosition0:1\n\nPosition0:5\n\nPosition6:1\n\nPosition2:7\n\nSo the number is 7 5 2 2 3 2 8 7 4 7.\n\nWait, let's write that as 9,502,844,731?\n\nWait, let's parse the digits properly:\n\nStarting from the left (billions place):\n\n3 (billions)\n\n7 (hundred millions)\n\n9 (ten millions)\n\n1 (millions)\n\n3 (hundred thousands)\n\n6 (ten thousands)\n\n3 (thousands)\n\n3 (hundreds)\n\n8 (tens)\n\n7 (units)\n\nWait, that would be 2,041,286,653.\n\nWait, but let me check that again. Let me count the digits:\n\nPosition24:6 (billions)\n\nPosition3:2 (hundred millions)\n\nPosition9:8 (ten millions)\n\nPosition6:4 (millions)\n\nPosition4:9 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition6:4 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition5:7 (thousands)\n\nPosition6:4 (hundreds)\n\nPosition9:1 (tens)\n\nPosition7:0 (units)\n\nSo yes, combining those digits:\n\n5 (billions), 8 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 4 (units).\n\nWhich is 0,204,537,136.\n\nWait, but let me verify with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, let me use another approach to cross-verify.\n\nLet me add 464,436,820 and 752,540,427.\n\nFirst, notice that 474 million plus 201 million is 6,060 million. Then, the remaining parts: 041,560 + 255,906.\n\n621,740 + 639,120.\n\nLet me compute that:\n\n777,778 + 573,231 = 6,336,182\n\nThen add 9,792: 5,281,391 +6,523 = 9,552,  (wait 4,223,382 +0,766: 6,128,468 +3,215=8,173,993; then +948 is 5,243,972 +125 = 2,382,  (wait 3,232,836 + 445 is 8,038,  (exact: 0,285,071 + 085 = 9,751,  (4,381,757 + 874=9,512,141; +70=5,343,232. So total is 6,355,436.\n\nTherefore,