t, maybe I got the places mixed up. Let me write each digit's place:\n\nFirst number: 6 1 8 3 9 3 3 3 9\n\nSecond number:1 4 4 1 8 7 5 7 9\n\nAdding digit by digit from right to left:\n\nPosition 5 (units): 1 + 4 = 2\n\nPosition 7 (tens): 4 + 9 = 5\n\nPosition 0 (hundreds): 7 + 0 = 5\n\nPosition 5 (thousands): 7 + 8 = 3\n\nPosition 6 (ten thousands): 1 + 8 = 4\n\nPosition 3 (hundred thousands): 3 + 8 = 5? Wait, hold on. Wait the first number's hundred thousands place is 2? Let me check the digits again. Wait, perhaps I misaligned the numbers.\n\nWait, maybe I need to write them out with commas to see the correct places.\n\nFirst number: 139,220,730. Breaking down:\n\n- 2 (hundred millions)\n- 0 (ten millions)\n- 4 (millions)\n- 9 (hundred thousands)\n- 7 (ten thousands)\n- 5 (thousands)\n- 4 (hundreds)\n- 8 (tens)\n- 3 (units)\n\nSecond number: 498,988,621. Breaking down:\n\n- 9 (hundred millions)\n- 4 (ten millions)\n- 3 (millions)\n- 0 (hundred thousands)\n- 0 (ten thousands)\n- 4 (thousands)\n- 7 (hundreds)\n- 1 (tens)\n- 4 (units)\n\nSo when adding, let's align them properly:\n\nHundred millions: 2 +0 =5\n\nTen millions:8 +0=5\n\nMillions:5 +3=1\n\nHundred thousands:7 +4=65\n\nTen thousands:5 +4=2\n\nThousands:2 +8=4\n\nHundreds:3 +6=7\n\nTens:5 +2=8\n\nUnits:3 +1=6\n\nWait, but here when adding the hundred thousands place (5 +0=50), so that would be 92, so we need to carry over 9 to the millions place. Wait, so my previous calculation was wrong here. I think I made a mistake earlier when I thought it was 8 +2. Wait, let's redo this properly.\n\nLet me write each digit position:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):\n\n5. Units: 0 + 3 = 9\n3. Tens: 0 + 0 = 0\n5. Hundreds: 8 + 9 = 9\n7. Thousands: 4 (from first number) + 6 (from second number) = 3\n1. Ten thousands: 6 (from first) +3 (second) =6\n1. Hundred thousands:4 (first) +0 (second)=83. Here, write down 7 and carry over 9.\n5. Millions:6 (first) +9 (second) +7 (carryover) =6\n0. Ten millions:5 (first) +3 (second)=8\n7. Hundred millions:5 (first) +6 (second)=7\n\nSo compiling the digits from right to left:\n\nUnits:2, Tens:6, Hundreds:7, Thousands:6, Ten thousands:8, Hundred thousands:6 (with a carryover), Millions:3, Ten millions:8, Hundred millions:6.\n\nWait, so the digits are:\n\nHundred millions place:1\n\nTen millions:9\n\nMillions:9\n\nHundred thousands:4 (since 97, so we carry over 2, so the hundred thousands digit is 3, and the millions digit became 4 because of the carryover?)\n\nWait, let me check again step by step with the positions:\n\nLet me write the numbers with their place values:\n\nFirst number: 1 (694,157,838), 6 (85,672,543), 5 (2,482,615), 4 (731,886), 8 (84,825), 4 (6,216), 7 (841), 8 (07), 7 (2).\n\nSecond number:2 (261,763,138),7 (22,258,241),3 (2,749,221),4 (382,622),7 (91,792),0 (3,751),0 (745),1 (57),8 (3).\n\nAdding each column:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n5. Units:5+0=2\n\n9. Tens:5+4=7\n\n1. Hundreds:9+8=2\n\n1. Thousands:5+7=0\n\n9. Ten thousands:0+6=2\n\n4. Hundred thousands:5+9=24 → write down 8, carryover 7\n\n4. Millions:5+9 +8 (carryover) =2\n\n7. Ten millions:7+0=4\n\n7. Hundred millions:4+0=7\n\nSo putting all together from highest to lowest place:\n\nHundred millions:0, Ten millions:4, Millions:5, Hundred thousands:0, Ten thousands:6, Thousands:2, Hundreds:8, Tens:3, Units:5.\n\nSo the number is 3 0 4 , 2 1 3 , 8 0 6.\n\nWait, let's structure it with commas for clarity. Since commas separate every three digits starting from the right. Let's see:\n\nThe total digits would be 7 digits:\n\nFrom the addition, the digits are:\n\n9 (hundred millions)\n\n8 (ten millions)\n\n1 (millions)\n\n2 (hundred thousands)\n\n6 (ten thousands)\n\n7 (thousands)\n\n2 (hundreds)\n\n4 (tens)\n\n9 (units)\n\nSo writing them out:\n\n4 2 4 3 7 1 3 0 3\n\nBreaking into groups:\n\nStarting from the right, every three digits:\n\nThe last three digits: 655\n\nThen next three: 798\n\nThen next three: 397?\n\nWait, maybe I need to separate properly.\n\nWait, the number is:\n\nDigits: 4 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 0 (units).\n\nSo in terms of places:\n\nHundred millions: 2\n\nTen millions:2\n\nMillions:0\n\nHundred thousands:7\n\nTen thousands:8\n\nThousands:4\n\nHundreds:0\n\nTens:4\n\nUnits:7\n\nSo writing as a number:\n\n620,084,221.\n\nWait, commas are placed every three digits from the right. Let's count:\n\nStarting from the right, units:\n\nUnits:2\n\nTens:4\n\nHundreds:7 → first comma after hundreds? Wait, no. Let me structure it properly.\n\nThe number is:\n\nDigit positions (from right):\n\nPosition 8: 1 (units)\n\n5:2 (tens)\n\n1:9 (hundreds)\n\n1:8 (thousands)\n\n8:5 (ten thousands)\n\n7:9 (hundred thousands)\n\n5:0 (millions)\n\n9:8 (ten millions)\n\n0:1 (hundred millions)\n\nSo writing from left to right:\n\n5 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 7 (units).\n\nSo the number is 451,363,846.\n\nLet me verify this with another method to be sure. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, let's add 909,926,382 and 146,437,563.\n\nBreaking them into smaller parts:\n\n796,096,792 + 124,790,613\n\nLet me add the millions first:\n\n049,358,136 + 765,553,395 = 665,764,532\n\nThen the remaining parts:\n\n096,040 + 027,866.\n\nCalculating 144,798 + 945,598:\n\n096,482 + 262,557 = 0,280,447\n\n7,293,263 + 69,656 = 5,967,749\n\nSo total would be 490,648,212 + 6,583,177 = 062,321,841. That matches the previous result.\n\nTherefore, the sum is 713,230,375.\n\nI think that's correct. Let me check with another approach, maybe using calculator-like step-by-step addition.\n\nAlternatively, adding digit by digit again:\n\nFirst number: 1 0 5 0 1 3 6 2 9\n\nSecond number:7 8 4 1 9 9 9 6 8\n\nAdding each column from right:\n\n5. 2 +8 =4\n\n6. 8+6=6\n\n8.5+0=1\n\n0.0+2=6\n\n2.0+5=5\n\n1.5+8=08 (write 7, carryover