3 2 5 7 7\n        ------------------------\n\nWait, actually, the subtrahend's digits should be aligned properly. Let me write each digit:\n\nStarting from the right (units):\n\nMinuend: 8 (units), 8 (tens), 5 (hundreds), 6 (thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 6 (hundred thousands), 7 (millions), 2 (ten millions), 8 (hundred millions).\n\nSubtrahend: 6 (units), 1 (tens),0 (hundreds),6 (thousands),4 (ten thousands),0 (hundred thousands),5 (millions),7 (ten millions),7 (hundred millions).\n\nSo subtraction digit by digit:\n\nStarting from units:\n\n5 - 5: borrow, 41-7=0. Borrow 0 from tens place.\n\nTens place: original 4 became 3 after borrow. Now 9 -6: need to borrow. Borrow from hundreds place.\n\nHundreds place:5 becomes 4, so tens place becomes 67. Now 54 (tens) -8=4. But the tens digit was 2 (after first borrow), so after borrowing, it's 21 (from hundreds) to tens, making it 95 in tens, subtract 9 gives 4. But the hundreds digit is now 3.\n\nHundreds place: 1 (after borrow) -5. Can't do, so borrow from thousands place.\n\nThousands place:5 becomes 2. Hundreds becomes 99 (7 +57). 56-8=6. \n\nThousands place is now 9 (after borrow). Subtract the subtrahend's thousands digit which is 0. 0-5: borrow again.\n\nBorrow from ten thousands place. Ten thousands digit is 3 becomes 2. Thousands becomes 67 (2 +75). 91-2=6.\n\nTen thousands place:7 (after borrow) -9. Can't do. Borrow from hundred thousands place.\n\nHundred thousands place:9 becomes 6. Ten thousands becomes 96 (8 +41). 98-5=3.\n\nHundred thousands place:0 (after borrow) -0. Can't do. Borrow from millions place.\n\nMillions place:6 becomes 3. Hundred thousands becomes 54 (5 +33). 59-9=0.\n\nMillions place:9 (after borrow) -6 (subtrahend's millions digit is 5). Can't do. Borrow from ten millions.\n\nTen millions place:0 becomes 4. Millions becomes 58 (3 +23). 69 -9=2.\n\nTen millions place:4 (after borrow) -5 (subtrahend's ten millions digit is 4). 1-5=4.\n\nHundred millions place:7 -3=6.\n\nPutting all together: t