m the right is the 0th digit: 2 (hundreds place). Fourth from right: 5 (thousands place). Fifth from right: 1 (ten thousands). Sixth from right:0 (hundred thousands). Seventh from right:3 (millions). Eighth from right:5 (ten millions). Ninth from right:8 (hundred millions).\n\nWait, that seems conflicting. Let me better write both numbers digit by digit, aligned properly.\n\nFirst number: 365,975,624\n\nDigits from left to right:\n\n6 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 7 (units).\n\nSecond number: 356,853,500\n\nDigits from left to right:\n\n8 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 0 (units).\n\nNow, aligning both numbers by their place values:\n\nHundred millions: 0 vs 3\n\nTen millions: 1 vs 5\n\nMillions:2 vs2\n\nHundred thousands:1 vs9\n\nTen thousands:1 vs6\n\nThousands:6 vs0\n\nHundreds:6 vs4\n\nTens:2 vs3\n\nUnits:3 vs2\n\nWait, but when adding, we need to start from the units and move left. Let me structure the addition vertically:\n\nLet me write both numbers vertically with each digit's place:\n\n          2  5  2  4  7  9  8  0  0\n        + 3  3  2  1  8  3  3  0  4\n        ---------------------------\nStarting from the right (units):\n\nPosition 2 (units): 9 +2 =25. Write 6, carryover 5.\n\nPosition 0 (tens):0 +7=06 +3=00. Write 1, carryover6.\n\nPosition8 (hundreds):3 +4=74 +4=84. Write 3, carryover2.\n\nPosition1 (thousands):8 +9=5 +0=8. Write0, no carryover.\n\nPosition1 (ten thousands):7 +5=3. Write8, no carryover.\n\nPosition1 (hundred thousands):8 +6=0. Write5, no carryover.\n\nPosition5 (millions):5 +9=83. Write3, carryover0.\n\nPosition9 (ten millions):7 +8=46 +8(carryover)=05. Write7, carryover9.\n\nPosition4 (hundred millions):5 +0=5 +4(carryover)=3. Write1.\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum would be:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:7, then 7, 5,4,0,2,7,0,5. Wait, but we have to consider the positions. Let's write the digits in order from highest to lowest place:\n\nThe result digits from position6 to position6:\n\nPosition4:7\n\nPosition7:3\n\nPosition8:3\n\nPosition3:8\n\nPosition4:5\n\nPosition7:1\n\nPosition1:3\n\nPosition0:5\n\nPosition7:6\n\nTherefore, the number is 5 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions),3 (millions),4 (hundred thousands),2 (ten thousands),3 (thousands),6 (hundreds),2 (tens),4 (units). So putting it all together:\n\n131,399,382.\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\nWait, the digits in each place:\n\nHundred millions place: 5\n\nTen millions place:3\n\nMillions place:1\n\nHundred thousands place:6\n\nTen thousands place:0\n\nThousands place:1\n\nHundreds place:3\n\nTens place:9\n\nUnits place:5\n\nSo the number would be 471,888,633.\n\nWait, let me verify this step by step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake in any of the positions.\n\nStarting over:\n\nAdding units:9+0=37. 7 carryover, digit 9.\n\nTens:6+8=54 +0=98 → digit8, carryover9.\n\nHundreds:0+7=09 +2=86 → digit8, carryover0.\n\nThousands:5+3=0 +9=0 → digit9, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands:3+2=1 → digit4, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands:0+2=9 → digit8, no carryover.\n\nMillions:9+5=25 → digit2, carryover4.\n\nTen millions:0+8=03 +2(carryover)=27 → digit7, carryover7.\n\nHundred millions:2+5=2 +2(carryover)=3 → digit1.\n\nSo the digits from highest to lowest:\n\nHundred millions:5\n\nTen millions:4\n\nMillions:9\n\nHundred thousands:3\n\nTen thousands:3\n\nThousands:5\n\nHundreds:3\n\nTens:1\n\nUnits:5\n\nTherefore, the number is 746,424,575.\n\nHmm, but let me check with another method to confirm. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, adding the two numbers:\n\n884,661,777 + 545,357,371.\n\nLet me add the millions first:\n\n478 million + 630 million = 839 million.\n\nThen the thousands: 515 thousand + 996 thousand = 473 thousand.\n\nThen the remaining part: 754 + 236 = 5,295.\n\nWait, hold on:\n\nWait, bre