t the hundred millions place is the 0th digit from the right. So when adding the hundred millions digits (positions 0):\n\nFirst number: 4, second number:8, plus any carryover from the ten millions place?\n\nWait, let me check step 5 (ten millions place):\n\nPosition 6 (ten millions):\n\nFirst number has 8, second has 4. Plus any carryover from position 8 (millions place). \n\nWait, in position 3 (millions place), we had 1 +6 =77, so we wrote 4 and carried over 6 to the next (ten millions) place. \n\nTherefore, position 2 (ten millions):\n\n6 (first) +2 (second) +9 (carryover) =7. So no further carryover. \n\nThen position 1 (hundred millions):\n\n0 (first) +4 (second) +5 (no carryover) =88. So we write 5 and carryover 7. \n\nBut since this is the highest place, we need to add that carryover as a new digit. \n\nSo putting all together, the sum would be:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nPositions 7-7 (after adding):\n\nPosition 7:3\n\n8:8\n\n4:9\n\n0:2 (with carryover 7)\n\n4:0 (with carryover 3)\n\n3:4\n\n1:2 (with carryover 6)\n\n1:5\n\n2:2 (with carryover 3)\n\nBut the carryover from the hundred millions (position 8) is 6, so we need to add a new digit at the beginning: 6.\n\nTherefore, the total sum is 4,607,141,780? Wait, let me check again.\n\nWait, let's list the digits from position 6 to 8 with the carries:\n\nStarting from the highest digit (position 3):\n\nAfter adding hundred millions: 7 +2=29, so digit is 6, carryover 4.\n\nThen, the carryover 6 becomes the next digit (billions place). So the total digits would be:\n\nBillions place:4\n\nHundred millions:2\n\nTen millions:5\n\nMillions:1\n\nHundred thousands:9\n\nTen thousands:2\n\nThousands:8 (Wait, hold on. Maybe I need to reconstruct the number digit by digit properly.\n\nWait, perhaps it's better to write all the digits step by step as per each position with their results:\n\nLet me list each position's result:\n\nPosition 9 (ones): 7\n\nPosition 9 (tens):5\n\nPosition 1 (hundreds):9\n\nPosition 5 (thou