gits from right to left (starting from ones to billions) are:\n\nOnes:8,\n\nTens:0,\n\nHundreds:9,\n\nThousands:0,\n\nTen thousands:3,\n\nHundred thousands:5,\n\nMillions:6,\n\nTen millions:4,\n\nHundred millions:8,\n\nBillions:3.\n\nWait, so arranging them in order from billions down to ones:\n\nBillions:8,\n\nHundred millions:5,\n\nTen millions:6,\n\nMillions:0,\n\nHundred thousands:4,\n\nTen thousands:7,\n\nThousands:2,\n\nHundreds:0,\n\nTens:4,\n\nOnes:4.\n\nSo the number is 0,489,337,831.\n\nWait, let me write that with commas for clarity: 8,189,055,139.\n\nHmm, let me verify this with another method to ensure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nLet me split the numbers into smaller chunks.\n\nFirst number: 723,376,772\n\nSecond number:543,355,073\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet's break them into millions and the rest.\n\nFirst number: 704,354,075 = 840,269,796 + 499,495\n\nSecond number:636,776,205 = 526,992,938 + 78,485\n\nAdding the millions parts: 504,577,151 +100,974,327 = 7,434,313,177\n\nAdding the smaller parts:554,676 +96,487.\n\nLet me compute that:\n\n901,294\n\n+ 91,485\n\n= ?\n\nAdding those:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n8 +1=85, write 4 carryover4.\n\n2+7=2 +4=6.\n\n2+2=2.\n\n4+9=6.\n\n4+6=1.\n\n2+7=2 (since 05,372 is 686,502 to match digits).\n\nWait, let me write them aligned:\n\n156,724\n\n+ 189,764\n\n= ?\n\nLet me add:\n\nOnes:1+7=51 →2, carryover0\n\nTens:8+7=1 +6=0\n\nHundreds:2+4=2\n\nThousands:6+1=7\n\nTen thousands:8+4=1\n\nHundred thousands:8+4=4\n\nMillions:5 (from 560,903) + 6 (from 420,318) but wait, 867,474 is 7.715 million? Wait no, perhaps better to do straight addition.\n\nWait, 801,659 is six hundred thirty-two thousand, three hundred forty-seven,\n\nplus thirty-two thousand, one hundred twenty-six.\n\nAdding:\n\n047,981\n\n+ 50,555\n\nStart from the right:\n\n3+8=71, carryover 9.\n\n7+4=2 +7=5.\n\n4+9=7.\n\n5+1=5.\n\n6 (ten thousands place of first number) +0 (ten thousands of second?) Wait