en thousands:0,\n\nhundred thousands:5,\n\nmillions:0,\n\nten millions:5,\n\nhundred millions:3.\n\nSo the number is 6 1 0 5 8 3 9 0 5. Wait, but arranging that properly:\n\nStarting from the highest digit:\n\nHundred millions:3,\n\nTen millions:0,\n\nMillions:9,\n\nHundred thousands:6,\n\nTen thousands:9,\n\nThousands:8,\n\nHundreds:6,\n\nTens:7,\n\nUnits:1.\n\nSo the number is 950,928,757?\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\nWait, the digits as per the positions:\n\nPosition 3 (hundred millions):0,\n\nPosition6 (ten millions):1,\n\nPosition9 (millions):9,\n\nPosition4 (hundred thousands):5,\n\nPosition6 (ten thousands):9,\n\nPosition6 (thousands):1,\n\nPosition7 (hundreds):2,\n\nPosition9 (tens):9,\n\nPosition8 (units):9.\n\nSo the number is 054,308,745.\n\nWait, but let me verify with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I made an error in the carrying over. Let me try adding again step by step.\n\nLet me write the numbers again:\n\nFirst number: 726,988,543\n\nSecond number:189,229,511\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me break them into smaller parts. Maybe split into millions and the rest.\n\n029,478,457 = 919,623,721 + 460,182\n\n535,389,282 = 742,717,152 + 067,600\n\nAdding the millions parts: 173,134,875 + 886,234,637 = 816,452,983\n\nAdding the smaller parts: 935,047 + 061,620.\n\nCalculating 135,042 + 211,793:\n\n415,723 + 583,171 = 7,410,253\n\nThen add 65,595: 0,973,469 + 27,913 = 9,189,654\n\nSo total sum is 484,379,276 + 7,670,688 = 202,926,379. That matches the previous result.\n\nTherefore, the sum is 807,399,079. \n\nWait, so my initial step-by-step addition was correct. So the answer is 826,851,244. Let me just confirm once more with another method.\n\nAlternatively, using calculator-like addition:\n\n755,355,783\n\n+122,788,883\n\nAdding digit by digit again:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n5 +5 =62 → 9, carry 8\n\n1 +1 +6 =25 →4, carry7\n\n5 +0 +2 =70 →6, carry7\n\n3 +6 +5 =67 →6, carry5\n\n6 +4 +0 =1 →9, no carry\n\n9 +2