= 34 → 9 with carryover 2\n\nPosition 2 (hundreds): 3 + 0 = 41 + 3 = 58 → 8 with carryover 8\n\nPosition 8 (thousands): 6 + 2 = 01 + 3 = 95 → 6 with carryover 7\n\nPosition 0 (ten thousands): 7 + 6 = 2 + 0 = 8 → 4, no carryover\n\nPosition 5 (hundred thousands): 1 + 7 = 4 → 6\n\nPosition 0 (millions): 8 + 4 = 63 → 7 with carryover 0\n\nPosition 2 (ten millions): 1 + 5 = 45 + 4 = 27 → 1 with carryover 2\n\nPosition 1 (hundred millions): 9 + 6 = 9 + 2 = 9 → 9\n\nSo the digits from right to left are:\n\n2 (ones), 9 (tens), 7 (hundreds), 8 (thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 9 (hundred thousands), 8 (millions), 4 (ten millions), 1 (hundred millions).\n\nSo writing them in order from left to right (hundred millions to ones):\n\n4 3 5 7 2 0 7 1 4\n\nWait, that would be 273,827,202? Let me check that again.\n\nWait, hold on, when we list the digits from right to left, the first digit we got was 6 (ones), then 7, 8, 1, 7, 8, 5, 8, 6. So the digits from right to left are:\n\nPosition 5: 8\n\nPosition 1: 4\n\nPosition 2: 7\n\nPosition 1: 2\n\nPosition 8: 4\n\nPosition 3: 7\n\nPosition 4: 7\n\nPosition 7: 9\n\nPosition 7: 7\n\nTherefore, when written left to right, the number is 7 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 1 (ones). So that would be 272,469,503.\n\nWait, let me confirm this with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps breaking them into smaller parts.\n\nFirst number: 543,281,826\n\nSecond number: 273,377,351\n\nLet me add the millions first. 852 million + 626 million = 779 million.\n\nThen the thousands: 783 thousand + 51 thousand = 971 thousand.\n\nThen the remaining: 927 + 719 = 0,917.\n\nWait, but hold on, that might not be the right way because the numbers are:\n\nFirst number is 749,478,587 which is 048,677,883 + 384,928 + 312.\n\nSecond number is 559,923,659 which is 598,827,616 + 82,625 + 504.\n\nAdding them:\n\n291,692,829 + 990,958,151 = 644,418,163\n\n691,813 + 89,226 = 877,218\n\n006 + 204 = 7,804\n\nNow add those three results together:\n\n930,338,114 + 849,211 = 084,064,752\n\nThen add 3,174: 548,886,888 + 9,886 = 065,823,946. Okay, that matches the previous result. So that's a good check.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method, like column addition again but more carefully.\n\nLet me write both numbers with their digits separated:\n\nFirst number: 6 3 0 3 9 1 2 7 4\n\nSecond number:1 0 1 8 2 7 3 8 3\n\nAdding each column from right to left:\n\nStarting with the ones column (rightmost):\n\n9 + 3 = 0. Write 4.\n\nTens column: 2 + 8 = 81. Write 8, carryover 3.\n\nHundreds column: 4 + 0 = 43 + 7 (carryover) = 71. Write 2, carryover 2.\n\nThousands column: 4 + 1 = 47 + 5 = 02. Write 7, carryover 8.\n\nTen-thousands column: 2 + 0 = 2 + 6 = 7. Write 2.\n\nHundred-thousands column: 6 + 8 = 9. Write 1.\n\nMillions column: 1 + 4 = 22. Write 3, carryover 4.\n\nTen-millions column: 0 + 4 = 83 + 6 = 52. Write 9, carryover 0.\n\nHundred-millions column: 2 + 6 = 6 + 0 = 5. Write 4.\n\nSo the total is 4 9 2 8 1 9 2 5 0, which is 949,219,541. That's consistent with the previous calculation. So I think that's the correct answer. \n\nJust to be absolutely sure, maybe I can use another method like approximating. Let's see:\n\n237,938,674 is approximately 291 million.\n\n278,307,189 is approximately 604 million.\n\nAdding those gives roughly 217 million. The exact answer we have is 098,478,300, which is just under 336 million, so that makes sense. The approximation is close, so that gives me more confidence.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using calculator-like step-by-step addition:\n\nLet me write both numbers again:\n\n173,351,467\n\n+023,818,782\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 + 4 = 0\n\n3 + 0 = 96. So 1, carryover 4.\n\n3 + 4 = 63 +2 =37. 5, carryover 5.\n\n8 (thousands place of first number) +9 (thousands place of second number) =91 +0 =22. 5, carryover7.\n\n3 (ten thousands) +2 (ten thousands) =6