dding digit by digit again to confirm.\n\nLet me write down the numbers again with commas for clarity:\n\n504,221,557\n\n066,665,737\n\nAdding digit by digit from right:\n\nOnes: 9 + 3 = 24 → 7, carryover 6\n\nTens: 5 + 9 = 8 +3=8 → 0, no carryover\n\nHundreds:3 +0=69 →1, carryover5\n\nThousands:8+4=70 +4=98 →5, carryover0\n\nTen thousands:2+7=0 +3=7 →7\n\nHundred thousands:1 +0=76 →6, carryover6\n\nMillions:1+8=93 +9=85 →0, carryover7\n\nTen millions:4 +2=88 +6=06 →8, carryover0\n\nHundred millions:9 +7=5 +5=0 →6\n\nSo writing all the digits from right to left: 6,2,9,0,5,4,1,2,5 → 130,228,399. Yep, same result.\n\nHmm, so I think that's correct. Maybe I can also use a calculator to verify, but since I don't have one here, my manual checks all lead to the same answer, so I feel confident it's 063,927,635.\n\nWait, just to ensure I didn't misalign any digits. Let me check the positions again.\n\nFirst number: 6 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 9 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 2 (hundred millions),8 (ten millions),6 (millions),1 (hundred thousands),0 (ten thousands),0 (thousands),4 (hundreds),8 (tens),1 (ones).\n\nYes, so when adding:\n\nHundred millions:7+9=5 plus carryover 6 makes 2. Correct.\n\nTen millions:2+8=51 plus carryover 6 makes 52. So digit 3, carryover6. Correct.\n\nMillions:6+9=23 plus carryover7 makes 85. So digit9, carryover7. Correct.\n\nHundred thousands:5+4=32 plus carryover0 makes 40? Wait, no, hold on. Wait, hundred thousands place: the first number's hundred thousands digit is 0 (since the number is 097,639,052: the digits are 8,9,2,0,6,6,4,9,3. The fourth digit from the right is thousands, so hundred thousands would be the fifth digit from the left? Wait, maybe I got the place values mixed up.\n\nWait, let me clarify the place values properly to ensure I didn't make a mistake in the digit positions.\n\nStarting from the right (units place):\n\nPosition