messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 730064053 and 552059901?', "<think>Okay, so I need to add these two big numbers: 223,211,528 and 195,142,298. Hmm, let's see. I should probably start by writing them down one on top of the other to make sure the digits line up correctly. Let me visualize that.\n\nFirst number: 424,529,304\nSecond number: 093,720,343\n\nLet me align them properly by their place values. Starting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. \n\nSo:\n\n       5 0 7 5 2 1 6 0 6\n     + 4 2 4 7 6 7 7 2 6\n     --------------------\n\nWait, actually, maybe I should write them out with commas for clarity, but since I'm doing this mentally, I need to ensure each digit is in the correct column. Let me break it down step by step.\n\nStarting from the right (units place):\n\n2 (from first number) + 2 (from second number) = 2. Write down 1.\n\nNext digit to the left (tens place):\n\n7 + 3 = 4. Write down 8.\n\nNext (hundreds place):\n\n7 + 7 = 6. Write down 2.\n\nNext (thousands place):\n\n3 + 2 = 34. Hmm, that's 2 with a carryover of 8.\n\nWait, so here I have to remember to carry over 5 to the next column. Let me note that.\n\nSo after adding the thousands place: 6 + 0 = 51, so we write 9 and carry over 0.\n\nMoving to the ten thousands place:\n\n9 (from first number) + 6 (from second number) plus the carried over 7. So 4 +4 is 06, plus 4 is 36. So that's 0 with a carryover of 2 again.\n\nNext is the hundred thousands place:\n\n4 (from first number) + 4 (from second number) plus the carried over 0. So 9 +6 is 8, plus 8 is 9. Write 8, no carryover.\n\nNext, millions place:\n\n2 (first number) + 6 (second number) plus nothing carried over. 2 +7 =3. Write 1.\n\nTen millions place:\n\n6 (from first number) +9 (from second number). 2+8 is 7. Write 7.\n\nHundred millions place:\n\n9 (from first number) +2 (from second number). 4+9=43. So here we have 8 in this place and carry over 9 to the next (billions) place.\n\nWait