ator-like addition.\n\nAlternatively, let me add the numbers digit by digit again step by step to ensure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n747,844,217\n\n+960,936,388\n\nLet me write them without commas for clarity:\n\n946453948\n\n+599003413\n\nAdding each digit from right:\n\nPosition 7 (ones):\n\n8 +1 =68. 3, carryover 8.\n\nPosition 4 (tens):\n\n0 +6 =5 +4=7. 7, carryover 3.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):\n\n2 +3=73. 7, carryover0.\n\nPosition3 (thousands):\n\n2 +2=99 +8=70. 5, carryover3.\n\nPosition8 (ten thousands):\n\n9 +3=1 +8=6. 2, carryover3.\n\nPosition8 (hundred thousands):\n\n9 +0=0. 9, carryover7.\n\nPosition7 (millions):\n\n8 +9=9. 2, carryover4.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):\n\n8 +7=99. 0, carryover0.\n\nPosition7 (hundred millions):\n\n3 +8=2 +4=4.\n\nSo writing all digits from right to left: 2,1,4,1,1,3,1,9,6.\n\nWhich is 8 2 5 6 5 6 3 3 9. Wait, positions:\n\nWait the digits would be:\n\nThe first digit (rightmost) is 8,\n\nthen 8,\n\nthen 2,\n\nthen5,\n\nthen5,\n\nthen4,\n\nthen4,\n\nthen8,\n\nthen3.\n\nSo the number is 2 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions),2 (millions),0 (hundred thousands),5 (ten thousands),4 (thousands),3 (hundreds),5 (tens),4 (ones). So that's 420,733,519. \n\nYes, that's the same as before. So I think that's correct. To be thorough, maybe approximate to check if it's reasonable.\n\n383 million plus 133 million is roughly 594 million. The extra parts are 419k and 903k, totaling about 202k. So total should be approximately 043,104,468. Since the exact is 565,703,626, which is very close, so that makes sense. The difference is because 890,987 +383,921 is exactly 290,199, so adding to 461,395,135 gives 606,763,521. \n\nTherefore, the answer should be 245,798,554. I don't see any mistakes in the steps. I think that's correct.\n</think>.\n\nThe sum of 252,128,435 and 685,718,605 is calculated as follows:.\n\n```.\n   252,128,435.\n+ 685,718,605.\n--------------.\n  937,847,040.\n```.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**.\n1.