ons:4\n\nSo the number is 5,104,263,425? Wait, let me arrange the digits properly.\n\nWait, the digits from highest to lowest:\n\nBillions place:7\n\nHundred millions:2\n\nTen millions:9\n\nMillions:5\n\nHundred thousands:2\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nThousands:4\n\nHundreds:2\n\nTens:8\n\nOnes:5\n\nSo combining these, it would be 9,790,852,211?\n\nWait, let me check with another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nFirst, let's consider 389,813,153 + 978,951,787.\n\nBreaking them into millions:\n\n007,573,874 is 597 million plus 006,149.\n\n887,859,889 is 371 million plus 260,859.\n\nAdding the millions: 669 + 908 = 0,756 million.\n\nThen adding the remaining parts: 568,382 + 133,779.\n\n036,363 + 374,315.\n\nLet me add those:\n\n170,500\n\n+295,806\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1+5=54 →3, carryover7\n\n5+3=5 +5=4 →1, no carry.\n\n7+8=91 →8, carryover0.\n\n4+2=9 +3=5 →9, no carry.\n\n3+3=41 →9, carryover7.\n\n8+7=9 +3=0 →7, no carry.\n\nSo that gives 154,404.\n\nWait, so adding 573,065 + 228,850 = 334,349?\n\nWait let me check again:\n\n810,870\n\n+505,009\n\nAdding the units:\n\nUnits:1+1=56, carryover5.\n\nTens:9+2=4+6=0.\n\nHundreds:0+6=76 →1 carryover8.\n\nThousands:7+1=5 +4=1.\n\nTen thousands:4+5=65 →2 carryover7.\n\nHundred thousands:4 (from 385,760's hundred thousands place is 1?) Wait, 977,590 is 3 (hundred thousands?), let me see:\n\nWait 063,279 is 9 (hundred thousand) place? Let's break down:\n\n622,518:\n\nDigit places:\n\nHundred thousands:9\n\nTen thousands:0\n\nThousands:8\n\nHundreds:8\n\nTens:1\n\nOnes:0\n\nWait, actually:\n\n656,775 is 0 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 0 (ones). So yes.\n\nSimilarly, 020,708 is 1 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\nAdding the hundred thousands: 7 +4 =3.\n\nTen thousands:2 +7=65 →1 with carryover0.\n\nThousands:9 +9=8 +2 (carryover) =6.\n\nHundreds:8 +6=89 →5 carry