:4\n\nTens:5\n\nUnits:3\n\nPutting it all together:\n\nBillions:2\n\nHundred millions:2\n\nTen millions:1\n\nMillions:6\n\nHundred thousands:2\n\nTen thousands:2\n\nThousands:4\n\nHundreds:7\n\nTens:3\n\nUnits:2\n\nSo the number is 4,938,947,216?\n\nWait, let's see:\n\nBreaking down:\n\nBillions digit:4\n\nThen hundred millions digit:7 → so that's 2,4...\n\nThen ten millions digit:8 → 0,93...\n\nMillions digit:5 → 8,411...\n\nHundred thousands digit:2 → 3,611,4...\n\nTen thousands digit:9 → 9,042,74...\n\nThousands digit:9 → 9,559,772...\n\nHundreds digit:9 → 9,541,484,1...\n\nTens digit:5 → 8,664,696,21...\n\nUnits digit:3 → 3,845,243,189.\n\nWait, so the total should be 6,850,842,338?\n\nWait, let me verify with another method. Maybe adding them in parts.\n\nAlternatively, 926,409,580 + 635,437,099.\n\nLet me split the numbers into millions for easier addition:\n\n496,471,417 = 250 million + 32,427\n\n968,797,693 = 668 million + 097,606\n\nAdding the millions: 219 + 332 = 5,719 million.\n\nAdding the remaining parts:01,414 + 940,804.\n\n67,335 + 457,569:\n\n67,525 + 943,733:\n\nAdding units:0+0=2\n\nTens:5+6=03 → 1 carryover8\n\nHundreds:5+4=74 +9=51 →3 carryover5\n\nThousands:2+8=3 +5=6\n\nTen thousands:6 (from 24,714 is 0 in the ten thousands place? Wait, 82,040 is 3 ten thousands, 8 thousand, 1 hundred, etc. Wait, 79,968 is 9 (ten thousands place?), no:\n\nWait 55,248 is:\n\nDigit breakdown:\n\n3 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 1 (units). So 5 ten thousand, 7 thousand, etc. So when adding to 788,807, which is 2 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 5 (units).\n\nWait, 986,332 is 6 (hundred thousand), 6 (ten thousand), 2 (thousand), 8 (hundred), 1 (ten), 3 (unit).\n\nSo adding 52,576 (which is 7 hundred thousands, 4 ten thousands, 3 thousands, 3 hundreds, 7 tens, 6 units) and 013,410 (7 hundred thousand, 6 ten thousands, 6 thousand, 2 hundreds, 3 tens, 5 unit):\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n    