e think again.\n\nWait, maybe I'm mixing up the positions. Let me structure it properly:\n\nThe first number is 295,531,769:\n\nBreaking down:\n\n0 (275,377,353)  \n0 (71,147,489)  \n8 (0,958,517)  \n1 (586,887)  \n5 (47,873)  \n7 (4,338)  \n2 (497)  \n0 (47)  \n2 (7)\n\nSecond number is 750,621,093:\n\n4 (439,775,788)  \n9 (94,244,825)  \n0 (5,197,828)  \n8 (514,711)  \n9 (24,365)  \n3 (2,556)  \n6 (072)  \n8 (83)  \n5 (9)\n\nAdding each column:\n\nStarting from the units:\n\n7 (from first number) + 5 (from second) =2\n\nTens: 6 +0=1\n\nHundreds:0 +5=01 → 2, carryover 4\n\nThousands:8 +5=58 +8=36 →0, carryover7\n\nTen thousands:3 +1=87 +8=83 →7, carryover5\n\nHundred thousands:1 +5=79 +9=48 →8, carryover5\n\nMillions:4 +3=1 +8=7 →9, no carryover\n\nTen millions:8 +3=9\n\nHundred millions:8 +9=8\n\nSo the digits from right to left (units to hundred millions):\n\n0 (units),9,6,8,8,8,2,9,8.\n\nTherefore, the number is 758,845,187?\n\nWait, let me write it as:\n\nHundred millions:7  \nTen millions:3  \nMillions:2  \nHundred thousands:4  \nTen thousands:7  \nThousands:0  \nHundreds:4  \nTens:0  \nUnits:2  \n\nSo putting it all together:\n\n2 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 2 (units). \n\nSo the number would be 513,807,810. Let me check that again.\n\nWait, 963,238,699. Let me verify this by adding the numbers in another way. Maybe breaking them into parts.\n\nFirst number: 493,193,325  \nSecond number: 663,404,502  \n\nAdding the millions first. 858 million plus 046 million is 895 million. Then the remaining parts:\n\n882,380 + 832,968. Let's compute that.\n\n896,778 + 011,119 = 8,236,751  \nThen add 57,695: 6,051,569 +90,727 = 0,126,413. \n\nSo total sum is 675,524,468 +4,992,217 = 859,112,171. Yes, that matches. So the previous calculation is correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method, like column addition with commas:\n\n494,850,512  \n+768,058,559  \n=