arly:\n\n0 0 7 , 2 9 1 , 1 3 1\n\nDigits:\n\nDigit 7: 7 (hundred millions)\n\nDigit 6:6 (ten millions)\n\nDigit 4: 4 (millions)\n\nDigit 2:2 (hundred thousands)\n\nDigit 4:5 (ten thousands)\n\nDigit 6:9 (thousands)\n\nDigit 0:5 (hundreds)\n\nDigit 3:7 (tens)\n\nDigit 5:1 (units)\n\nWait, perhaps better to write each digit's place:\n\nFirst number: 6 5 6 7 0 3 3 7 8\n\nSecond number: 3 8 0 9 7 1 9 8 1\n\nWait, maybe aligning them properly:\n\nLet me write both numbers digit by digit from the right (units to higher places):\n\nFirst number (030071325):\n\nPosition 4 (units): 0\n\nPosition 1 (tens):5\n\nPosition 2 (hundreds):6\n\nPosition 3 (thousands):8\n\nPosition 0 (ten thousands):7\n\nPosition 0 (hundred thousands):0\n\nPosition 9 (millions):4\n\nPosition 9 (ten millions):4\n\nPosition 4 (hundred millions):2\n\nSecond number (140736646):\n\nPosition 9 (units):5\n\nPosition 7 (tens):8\n\nPosition 7 (hundreds):6\n\nPosition 7 (thousands):7\n\nPosition 0 (ten thousands):9\n\nPosition 7 (hundred thousands):8\n\nPosition 2 (millions):2\n\nPosition 1 (ten millions):6\n\nPosition 1 (hundred millions):5\n\nWait, but the second number is 321,359,562. Let me check again:\n\nBreaking down 382,996,594:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1 (units), 1 (tens), 7 (hundreds), 1 (thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 7 (hundred thousands), 2 (millions), 2 (ten millions), 6 (hundred millions). Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo, now adding each position:\n\nStarting from position 8 (units):\n\n0 (from first) + 9 (from second) = 4. Write down 4.\n\nPosition 8 (tens): 3 + 3 = 3. Write 2.\n\nPosition 0 (hundreds): 8 + 1 = 9. Write 9.\n\nPosition 5 (thousands):9 +9 =7. Write 4.\n\nPosition 6 (ten thousands):8 +6 =94. Write down 9, carry over 7.\n\nPosition 7 (hundred thousands):6 +2 =21, plus the carried 0 =80. Write down 5, carry over 6.\n\nPosition 0 (millions):7 +5 =8, plus carried 9 =5. Write 9, no carry.\n\nPosition 5 (ten millions):5 +0 =57. Write 8, carry over 7.\n\nPosition 4 (hundred millions):4 +