method suggested 4,734,893,960, which is exactly 4,683,658 difference.\n\nWait, let me check with another approach: using calculator-like step.\n\nLet me add the two numbers:\n\n053,745,589\n\n+562,988,974\n\n-------------\n\nLet me add the numbers step by step:\n\nFirst, add 957,788,776 + 057,667,399 = 3,735,000,644\n\nThen add the remaining 21,005,008:\n\n5,942,417,002 + 30,765,293\n\n= 4,642,514,663 + 46,484,827 = 3,220,633,564\n\nThen +9,164,349:\n\n4,982,281,163 + 5,168,903 = ?\n\nAdding 2,221,784: 4,366,037,724\n\nThen +775,514:\n\n7,521,938,886 + 087,404 = 6,221,278,460.\n\nAh! So this gives the correct approximate result of 2,854,132,511, which matches the approximate calculation. But my digit-by-digit addition gave 8,196,237,517. There's a discrepancy here. Therefore, I must have made a mistake in my digit-by-digit addition.\n\nLet me go back to the digit-by-digit steps and see where I went wrong.\n\nLet me write down the two numbers aligned properly:\n\n          3 2 8 6 0 4 3 7 0\n        + 6 7 5 5 9 4 7 5 0\n        --------------------\n\nLet me write them vertically with each digit aligned:\n\nHundred millions: 9 +0\n\nTen millions:5 +1\n\nMillions:0 +2\n\nHundred thousands:6 +3\n\nTen thousands:4 +3\n\nThousands:7 +8\n\nHundreds:7 +9\n\nTens:0 +9\n\nUnits:9 +1\n\nWait, perhaps I mixed up the digit positions earlier. Let me realign:\n\nWait, perhaps my earlier breakdown was wrong. Let me re-express each number with their digit places clearly.\n\nFirst number: 241,591,332\n\nBreaking down each digit from left (billions) to right (units):\n\nDigit 2 (hundred millions place):1\n\nDigit 0 (ten millions):9\n\nDigit5 (millions):7\n\nDigit6 (hundred thousands):4\n\nDigit4 (ten thousands):8\n\nDigit0 (thousands):0\n\nDigit9 (hundreds):6\n\nDigit6 (tens):1\n\nDigit3 (units):0\n\nSecond number:165,345,472\n\nDigit8 (hundred millions):2\n\nDigit7 (ten millions):5\n\nDigit5 (millions):2\n\nDigit3 (hundred thousands):0\n\nDigit0 (ten thousands):5\n\nDigit5 (thousan