ns place and carryover2 to the billions place. Since there are no higher digits, the carryover becomes a new digit at the beginning. So the total would be 6 (billion), 1 (hundred millions), then the rest of the digits.\n\nPutting it all together from left to right:\n\nStarting with the carryover 6 (billions place), then the hundred millions digit is 7, ten millions is7, millions is9, hundred thousands is7, ten thousands is2, thousands is2, hundreds is9, tens is2, units is3.\n\nWait let me list each position's result from highest to lowest:\n\nBillions place:8\n\nHundred millions:3\n\nTen millions:1\n\nMillions:1\n\nHundred thousands:5\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nThousands:8\n\nHundreds:5\n\nTens:6\n\nUnits:9\n\nTherefore, combining these digits:\n\n6 (billion), 4 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 2 (units). So the number is 9,334,812,734.\n\nWait, let me check this again step by step:\n\nStarting from the highest place (billions):\n\n2\n\nThen hundred millions:3 → 8,0...\n\nTen millions:1 → 5,88...\n\nMillions:9 → 9,384...\n\nHundred thousands:7 → 9,333,9...\n\nTen thousands:2 → 2,797,04...\n\nThousands:0 → 3,701,813...\n\nHundreds:1 → 7,928,071,8...\n\nTens:1 → 9,276,311,07...\n\nUnits:0 → 8,358,358,072.\n\nYes, that seems right. Let me verify with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, I can add 665,154,926 + 565,067,948.\n\nLet me try adding them in chunks.\n\nFirst, add the millions:\n\n485,057,188 is 050 million plus 370,822.\n\n748,711,482 is 276 million plus 602,837.\n\nAdding the millions parts: 470 + 667 = 7,452 million.\n\nThen adding the remaining parts: 513,851 + 432,988.\n\nLet me compute that:\n\n475,052 + 925,882.\n\nAdding those:\n\n406,192\n\n+911,492\n\n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n3 +5=94, write4 carry3.\n\n1 +1 +3=81, write4 carry2.\n\n2 +0 +0=8, write1.\n\n9+9=0.\n\n6+9=91, write6 carry2.\n\n6+7 +3=68, write1 carry3.\n